  <div class="guide-text-block">
    <h2>The Science of Aggregate Bulk Density</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Bulk density</strong> (also called "unit weight") is the weight of aggregate per unit of volume, including spaces between particles. <a href="https://store.astm.org/c0029_c0029m-23.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">ASTM C29/C29M</a> and AASHTO T 19 describe methods for measuring it in loose or compacted test samples. They do not assign a fixed density to each material. ASTM also notes that dry test values may differ from moist material in a stockpile or hauling unit.
    </p>
    <p>
      Understanding bulk density is vital because materials are bought and sold across two different physical metrics: landscape drawings specify <strong>volume (cubic yards)</strong>, whereas quarries bill clients by <strong>weight (short tons of 2,000 pounds)</strong> across certified platform scales.
    </p>

